================================================================================
Fix: a run covers the rules that were picked, and only those
================================================================================

Context:
Choosing a few rules still ran everything. SHACL shapes have a checkbox each,
but SWRL rules, decision tables and aggregate rules did not: they had no id to
be addressed by, so a run pulled them in whole whenever their dimension was
selected. A dimension counts as selected while it is checked *or*
indeterminate, so unticking all but one Conformance rule left Conformance
indeterminate and ran every decision table and aggregate rule, while Structural
stayed checked and ran every SWRL rule.

They are now selected exactly as shapes are, by the same check id the run
already reports them under (`swrl:<name>`, `dt:<name>`, `agg:<name>`).

Changes:
1. `src/back/core/w3c/shacl/constants.py`
   Added the family id prefixes, `RULE_FAMILY_CATEGORIES` and `rule_check_id()`
   so the list endpoint, the run selection and the reported result derive the
   id in one place — if they disagree a rule silently cannot be picked.
2. `src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py`
   `/ontology/dataquality/list` gains a `rules` key holding the three families
   as selectable entries. `shapes` is left untouched because the ontology
   editor reads the same endpoint and manages actual shapes only.
3. `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py`
   `start_dataquality_checks()` filters each family by check id when rules are
   named, falling back to the dimension when they are not, and stamps the
   resolved `check_id` on each rule it passes on.
4. `src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py`
   The three family loops resolve their id once through `_rule_check_id()`,
   which prefers the stamped value: filtering renumbers the list, so an
   unnamed rule would otherwise report its neighbour's id.
5. `src/front/static/query/js/query-dataquality.js`
   `_loadShapes()` merges `rules` into the shape cache, so each one renders a
   checkbox under its dimension and travels in `shape_ids` when ticked.
6. `tests/units/api/test_dq_rule_list.py`
   New module: the families are offered with the ids the runner reports, the
   shapes list stays free of them, disabled rules are not offered, and the
   runner agrees with the selector on the id.
7. `tests/units/api/test_dq_run_selection.py`
   New `TestRuleSelection` cases: a SWRL rule can be picked on its own,
   unpicking one rule of a family keeps the others, and a ticked dimension no
   longer drags its rules in. Replaced the case that asserted the old
   behaviour.
8. `tests/units/front/test_dq_rule_checkboxes.py`
   New node-executed module asserting a SWRL rule and a decision table each
   render a checkbox under their dimension, and that a response with no
   `rules` key still works.

